  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Geometry on the EST I covers areas, perimeters, volumes, and coordinate geometry. A reference sheet of key formulas is provided on the test.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle area",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\pi r^2 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circumference",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( 2\\pi r \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Pythagorean theorem",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( a^2+b^2=c^2 \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Distance",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{(x_2-x_1)^2+(y_2-y_1)^2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 6.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A right triangle has legs \\( 6 \\) and \\( 8 \\). Find the hypotenuse. \\[ c=\\sqrt{6^2+8^2}=\\sqrt{36+64}=\\sqrt{100}=10. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · The Pythagorean theorem",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "estPythCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A right triangle with squares built on each side, showing that the two smaller squares' areas add to the largest",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "estPythDataBtn",
          "panelId": "estPythDataPanel",
          "descId": "estPythDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "estPythDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "The two legs, the hypotenuse, and their squares",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "quantity",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "value",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "estLegA",
            "valueDisplayId": "estLegAlab",
            "label": {
              "en": "leg <b>a</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Leg a",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 2,
            "max": 8,
            "value": 6,
            "step": 1
          },
          {
            "id": "estLegB",
            "valueDisplayId": "estLegBlab",
            "label": {
              "en": "leg <b>b</b>:",
              "ar": null
            },
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Leg b",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 2,
            "max": 8,
            "value": 8,
            "step": 1
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "estA2B2",
            "label": {
              "en": "a² + b²",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo"
          },
          {
            "id": "estC2",
            "label": {
              "en": "c² (hypotenuse²)",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "estHyp",
            "label": {
              "en": "c",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "The blue and amber squares' areas always sum to the dark square's area — that's exactly \\(a^2+b^2=c^2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "<h3>Coordinate geometry</h3>The midpoint of \\( (x_1,y_1) \\) and \\( (x_2,y_2) \\) is \\( \\left(\\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2},\\dfrac{y_1+y_2}{2}\\right) \\). A circle with centre \\( (h,k) \\) and radius \\( r \\) satisfies \\( (x-h)^2+(y-k)^2=r^2 \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Geometry — Key Formulas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Triangle area \\(= \\tfrac{1}{2}bh\\). Circle area \\(= \\pi r^2\\), circumference \\(= 2\\pi r\\). Trapezoid area \\(= \\tfrac{1}{2}(a+b)h\\). Cylinder volume \\(= \\pi r^2 h\\). Cone volume \\(= \\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h\\). Sphere volume \\(= \\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\). <strong>Angle sum:</strong> triangle 180°; quadrilateral 360°; \\(n\\)-gon \\((n-2) \\times 180°\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Similar triangles",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Triangles \\(ABC\\) and \\(DEF\\) are similar. \\(AB = 6\\), \\(DE = 9\\), \\(BC = 8\\). Find \\(EF\\). <p>Scale factor \\(k = 9/6 = 1.5\\). \\(EF = 8 \\times 1.5 = 12\\).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A rectangle has perimeter 48 cm and length twice its width. Find its area.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Let width \\(= w\\). \\(2(2w+w)=48 \\Rightarrow 6w=48 \\Rightarrow w=8\\). Length \\(=16\\). Area \\(= 128\\) cm\\(^2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
